45030054450035, 0.029148845002055168, 0.007141995243728161, 0.019683390855789185, 0.04477938637137413]], "input": ["# Otolaryngology Service and Dysphagia Management\n\nThe community is centered around the Otolaryngology Service, which specializes in ear, nose, and throat disorders, particularly focusing on dysphagia management. Key entities include C. Morera Pérez, D. Escollado, and J. M. Perolada, all of whom are involved in providing recommendations for medication administration and improving patient care related to swallowing disorders.\n\n## Central role of the Otolaryngology Service\n\nThe Otolaryngology Service is the primary entity in this community, specializing in disorders related to the ear, nose, and throat, with a significant focus on dysphagia. This service plays a crucial role in diagnosing and treating conditions that affect swallowing, which can have serious implications for patient health. The service's comprehensive approach to managing these disorders is vital for improving patient outcomes and ensuring effective treatment protocols. [Data: Entities (2916); Relationships (10736, 10735, +more)]\n\n## C. Morera Pérez's contributions\n\nC. Morera Pérez is a key member of the Otolaryngology Service, specializing in dysphagia treatments and medication administration through enteral feeding. This dual focus highlights a commitment to enhancing patient care for those with swallowing difficulties. Morera Pérez's involvement in recommendations for medication administration is particularly important, as it ensures that patients receive appropriate and effective treatment tailored to their specific needs. [Data: Entities (2929); Relationships (7907, 10737, +more)]\n\n## D. Escollado's expertise\n\nD. Escollado is another vital member of the Otolaryngology Service, focusing on dysphagia-related issues and medication administration via enteral feeding. Escollado's work is essential in providing a comprehensive approach to managing patients with swallowing di